      "id": "17881",
      "key": "SFCC-45",
      "summary": "Currency Conversion Approach Configuration",
      "description": "As a\n Site Admin, \n\n\nI want\n to configure the currency conversion approach, rounding rules, and BM admin interface per currency in SFCC Business Manager, \n\n\nso that\n prices in non-base currencies are calculated consistently and correctly per market.\nConversion approaches: \nBase RRP\n — no conversion; currency matches the storefront base pricebook\nFixed Pricelist\n — price loaded directly from AP21 per market (see \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-36\n )\nFixed FX Rate\n — base price multiplied by a configured fixed FX rate\nDynamic FX Rate\n — base price multiplied by the nightly rate retrieved from Global-e (see \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-47\n)\n\n\nRounding rules\n: A rounding strategy is applied per currency (e.g. nearest whole AED, 2 decimal places EUR, 0 decimal places JPY). Rounding is configurable per currency and applied at line-item level before tax or promotion stacking.\nBM must provide a role-controlled interface for authorised users to view and update the conversion approach per currency and view the current FX rate, last-updated timestamp, and feed status (success / stale / failed) from the Global-e nightly feed.\nBulk import and export of currency configuration (conversion approach, per-currency settings, and rounding rules) must be supported for technical users via SFCC Site Import/Export, OCAPI, or deployment scripts.",
