      "id": "19426",
      "key": "SFCC-863",
      "summary": "Suppress placeholder DntNotification modal; route consent through Didomi",
      "description": "Context\nSurfaced while investigating SFCC-860's Lighthouse \ncategories.performance\n finding (LCP 6.4s / score 0.1) against a real deployed build. The Largest Contentful Paint element turned out not to be an image — the homepage currently has none — but literal placeholder text inside a modal:\n\"Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua...\"\nTraced to \n@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/hooks/use-dnt-notification.js\n's \nDntNotification\n component, rendered unconditionally in the \nbase\n \n_app/index.jsx\n (\n<DntNotification {...dntNotification} />\n) — Zimmermann has no override for \n_app\n yet, so this base behaviour is live as-is on every tier. Salesforce's own source comment confirms it's not meant to ship: \n// Placeholder for the consent tracking form for demonstration purposes\n.\nIt auto-opens via a \nuseEffect\n whenever \nselectedDnt === undefined\n (i.e. on every fresh session with no stored preference — \nselectedDnt\n comes from \nuseDNT()\n's \nauth.getDnt()\n, reading the real SLAS/DNT cookie, so there is no config-level default that suppresses the auto-open; confirmed no \ngetConfig()?.app?.dntNotificationEnabled\n-style toggle exists, unlike e.g. \nstoreLocatorEnabled\n). That's exactly why a fresh, cookie-less Lighthouse run measures it as the LCP element — it's the first substantial content to appear.\nWhy this matters beyond performance\nPer \nAGENTS.md\n's Consent & Marketing section, Didomi is meant to own all consent gating for this project (\n.docs/memory/projectState.md\n lists Didomi integration as not-yet-started, REG-054). This base component is not that — it's Salesforce's own demo scaffolding, and real shoppers on any tier without an \n_app\n override are currently seeing literal \"Lorem ipsum\" copy in a tracking-consent dialog. This is a live UX/compliance bug, not just a Lighthouse number.\nScope\nOverride \noverrides/app/components/_app/index.tsx\n (Tier 2 — Global Shell, \"Both Squads — coordinate before touching\" per \nprotectedFiles.md\n; copy-first from \nnode_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/components/_app/index.jsx\n per \nAGENTS.md\n's Copy-first rule) to stop rendering \n<DntNotification>\nHeader\n and \nFooter\n are both already overridden (\noverrides/app/components/header/\n, \noverrides/app/components/footer/\n) — the new \n_app\n override must import them via relative paths (\n../header\n, \n../footer\n), not the base SFCC path, per \n.claude/rules/overrideStyling.md\n's \"Importing an already-overridden component from a new component\" section, or Storybook/Vitest will silently exercise the unstyled base versions\nDecide how this interacts with the broader Didomi integration (REG-054) — does DNT tracking-consent get replaced by a Didomi-driven flow entirely, or does this story just remove the placeholder and Didomi work supersedes it later?\nFull TypeScript port of \n_app\n is non-trivial: ~500 lines, many hooks (\nuseAuthModal\n, \nuseStoreLocatorModal\n, \nuseMultiSite\n, \nuseUpdateShopperContext\n, \nPageDesignerProvider\n, \nCurrencyProvider\n, checkout header/footer variants, etc.) — budget real review time, not a quick patch\nAcceptance criteria\nNo placeholder/demo consent copy is ever shown to a real shopper on any tier\nLighthouse's LCP on the homepage reflects real content, not this modal\nHeader/Footer overrides continue to render correctly through the new \n_app\n override (spot-check Storybook and the real app, not just tsc)",
