      "id": "19418",
      "key": "SFCC-857",
      "summary": "Enhancement – Emarsys Web Extend Integration (Cart Abandonment, Browse Abandonment & Revenue Tracking)",
      "description": "Epic\nSFCC-24 – Enhancements\nBackground\nZimmermann currently uses Emarsys Web Extend on Magento to power three CRM flows: \ncart abandonment\n, \nbrowse abandonment\n, and \nrevenue contribution reporting\n. These are direct browser-side integrations (3rd party JavaScript injection) and are separate from the client data CRM integration, which runs via Omneo → Mulesoft → Emarsys.\nBoth integrations must be replicated in SFCC — this story covers the \nWeb Extend\n (JavaScript/browsing data) integration only. The Omneo/Mulesoft client data sync is covered separately.\nSAP Emarsys Web Extend documentation shared by Tessa Turnbull (Global CRM Director):\nhttps://help.sap.com/docs/SAP_EMARSYS/5d44574160f44536b0130abf58cb87cc/fdf50dbc74c1101495318ae4e0236a67.html?locale=en-US\n \nhttps://help.sap.com/docs/SAP_EMARSYS/5d44574160f44536b0130abf58cb87cc/0e098e6a840d4832a0775b5acb0d24af.html?locale=en-US\n \nKnown Use Cases (in scope for analysis)\nCart Abandonment\n – Emarsys sends a reminder email when a customer adds items to bag but does not complete checkout.\nBrowse Abandonment\n – Emarsys sends a reminder email featuring a product the customer viewed but did not add to bag.\nRevenue Contribution Reporting\n – Web Extend captures revenue data for CRM reporting purposes.\nOutstanding Questions (to be resolved before story can be refined)\nThe following questions were raised by Jasmijn Tsang (6 July 2026) and have \nnot yet been answered\n by Zimmermann:\nCart Abandonment – customer scope\n: Is this triggered for logged-in customers only, or does it also apply to guest customers who have entered their email address at checkout entry?\nBrowse Abandonment – customer scope\n: Is this working for logged-in customers only, or does it also apply to customers identified via a cookie from a previous session?\nAdditional CRM flows\n: Are there any other CRM flows powered by Web Extend beyond the three identified above?\nTechnical Considerations\nWeb Extend is a \n3rd party JavaScript injection\n — scripts will need to be loaded on relevant SFCC pages.\nTNL responsibility\n: Confirm whether TNL (Zimmermann's team) will be configuring the rules, loading logic, and maintaining the Data Dictionary for click events and abandon events. Accenture to confirm scope boundary.\nData Dictionary\n: Click Event and Abandon Event capture will need to be defined.",
