      "id": "18317",
      "key": "SFCC-191",
      "summary": "Cart - Promo Code Entry & Validation",
      "description": "As a \nShopper, \nI want\n to enter a promotional code on the cart page and receive immediate feedback on whether it is valid, \nso that\n I can apply eligible discounts to my order before proceeding to checkout.\nThe promo code section is displayed as a collapsed accordion on the cart page. This story covers the entry mechanism, validation feedback, confirmation messaging, applied state display (including the applied code label and Remove interaction), Apply button disable state after a successful application, and item-level discount display. Once a promo code is successfully applied, the Apply button is disabled — preventing a second code from being entered. Auto-applied discounts (e.g. customer group discounts such as Gold VIC) are displayed in the same discounts area — their rendering is handled in \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-38\n and \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-42\n. For international (Global-e) checkouts, coupon validation occurs in SFCC before cart handoff — Global-e does not re-validate. Promotion calculations execute in the customer's selected ship-to currency. Promo codes and discount values must be included in the Global-e cart payload — see PRC-43/PRC-46 and the broader Global-e cart handoff story.\nThis story covers the promo code entry flow and validation logic, including the accordion UI, Apply/Remove interactions, error messaging, and applied state. The rendering of Was/Now pricing and item-level discount labels (e.g. \"20% off applied\") on cart line items is not in scope here — that is covered in \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-795\n. The promotional banner is covered in \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-404\n.\nReference images (Figma is leading):\nAccordion closed:\n\n\nAccordion open:\nCode applied (Apply greyed out):\nError message:",
