      "id": "18376",
      "key": "SFCC-198",
      "summary": "Promotions – Promotion Calculation in Target Currency",
      "description": "As a\n Site Merchandiser, \nI want\n all promotion discounts to be calculated correctly in the shopper's target currency, \nso that\n savings are accurate regardless of the market the shopper is purchasing from.\nThis story covers SFCC-side configuration and custom logic required to ensure all promotion types calculate correctly in the shopper's selected ship-to currency. Percentage discount promotions are applied post-FX conversion against the converted price. Fixed-amount promotions must either be defined per currency in BM or use a base-currency equivalent converted using the configured FX rate with a documented rounding rulei. Rounding rules per currency are applied after all discount calculations, per the configuration in SFCC-45. Custom logic is required to enforce target-currency calculation behaviour as this is not SFCC default. Depends on SFCC-45 (Currency Conversion Approach Configuration) and SFCC-47 (Global-e FX & Pricing Job).",
