      "id": "19262",
      "key": "SFCC-778",
      "summary": "Customer Group Pricing — Catalogue Price Rule Display",
      "description": "As a \nShopper, \nI want\n promotional pricing configured via a catalogue price rule to display correctly across PLP, PDP, cart, and checkout, \nso that \nI see accurate discounted prices wherever I browse without needing to enter a code or reach the cart.\nWhen a catalogue price rule promotion is active and a Shopper is logged in, Was/Now pricing is displayed on PLP (via the product card) and PDP. In cart and checkout, Was/Now pricing is also shown, accompanied by a promotional label (e.g. \"Private Sale — 20% Off Applied\") indicating the discount has been applied.\nThis differs from a standard sale, which is driven by a sale pricebook and does not require login. Catalogue price rules may or may not be group-restricted depending on BM configuration — any logged-in customer may see the pricing. The EU domestic private sale is an example of this promotion type.\nWhere a catalogue price rule and a cart price rule are both active on the same storefront simultaneously, double discounts can occur unless product/season scope is explicitly managed in BM. This is Zimmermann's responsibility — see Dependencies.\nBM configuration of a test catalogue price rule is covered in SFCC-38. Global-e support for catalogue price rules on international storefronts is unconfirmed — see Dependencies.",
